11486268,2025-01-13,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"Dear XXXX, I am writing to file a formal complaint against XXXX for XXXX in unfair and deceptive practices that violate the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), including laws related to identity theft and the re-insertion of fraudulent information. XXXX actions have caused significant harm to my financial well-being, severely impacting my ability to obtain credit, housing, and employment. 
1. Re-insertion of Fraudulent Accounts Due to Identity Theft XXXX has repeatedly reinserted fraudulent accounts on my credit report that were the result of identity theft. These accounts were previously deleted after I disputed their accuracy and provided sufficient documentation proving that I was not responsible for the fraudulent activity. Despite this, XXXX has placed these fraudulent accounts back onto my credit report without proper verification or documentation, in violation of my rights under the FCRA and identity theft protections. 
Under the FCRA, Section 605B specifically addresses fraudulent information resulting from identity theft. This section mandates that any information reported on a credit report that has been identified as fraudulent due to identity theft must be blocked upon receipt of a consumer 's identity theft report. Despite this, XXXX has failed to block fraudulent accounts tied to identity theft and has reinserted them into my report, causing me substantial harm. 
2. Failure to Delete Inaccurate and Incomplete Information In addition to the re-insertion of fraudulent accounts, XXXX has failed to properly delete inaccurate and incomplete information and addresses from my credit report. This includes information that has been proven to be erroneous through prior disputes and investigations. As a result, inaccurate data remains on my credit file, violating XXXX 's obligations under the FCRA to ensure that the information is accurate, complete, and up-to-date. 
XXXX. Damaging My Credit and Livelihood As a direct result of these actions, my credit report has been severely damaged, making it incredibly difficult for me to obtain credit, secure housing, or even find stable employment. The inaccurate and incomplete information on my credit report has caused financial distress and has significantly hindered my ability to maintain stable living and employment conditions. These actions by XXXX are causing ongoing damage to my livelihood, which has already been affected by identity theft. 
4. Violations of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) Experians actions are in clear violation of several key provisions of the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), including the following : Section 611 : Procedures in case of disputed information XXXX has failed to follow proper procedures for investigating and correcting disputed information, especially regarding fraudulent accounts that were previously removed.

